   "text": "# term-weave\n\n## What it does\n\nDrafts a glossary of project terms from Markdown and plain-text documents in a supplied folder. Every drafted definition links to the passage that supports it.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it when project vocabulary is scattered across documents or newcomers encounter unexplained terms.\n\n## How it works\n\nRun the skill manually:\n\n```text\n/term-weave <source-folder>\n```\n\nIt reads Markdown and plain-text documents and ignores other file types. If the folder is missing or contains no readable supported documents, it stops and explains the problem without drafting.\n\nIt does not invent definitions. Terms without a supporting explanation appear under **Unresolved terms**. When sources conflict, it preserves both definitions in one entry, links each source, and marks the entry **Conflict**.\n\n## What you get\n\nA `GLOSSARY.md` file in the working directory, with entries sorted alphabetically and **Unresolved terms** after the defined entries. The source documents remain unchanged.",
